 "observations": [
  "col_left L1: the line continues the entry Vettius Valens of p. 411. The small-capital L of «{sc:lxxix}» is printed broken, like ı.",
  "col_left L9: «*Vocabulista in Arabico*» is printed in italics. A speck over the first 2 of «202» is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L10: «*al-‘awāmm*» is printed in italics, with the sign of ‘ayn and the bar over the a.",
  "col_left L11, L12, L33, L34, L35: a space of two blank lines (41.6 points from baseline to baseline) separates the names in V from those in W; the names in W, X and Y are separated by somewhat less (34.3 and 35.4 points).",
  "col_left L13: «Wālīs» has the bars over the a and the i (the bar over the i 2.4 by 1.2 points).",
  "col_left L14: «al-Wānsharīshī» has the bars over the a and over the second and the last i; «Saḥnūn» the dot under the h and the bar over the u; «‘Othmān» the sign of ‘ayn and the bar over the a.",
  "col_left L15: «al-Wāqidī» has the bar over the a, a round dot on the i after the q (1.6 by 1.6 points) and the bar over the last i.",
  "col_left L16: «Waṭwāṭ» has the dots under both t and the bar over the second a.",
  "col_left L22, L26: the lower right end of the foot of the small-capital L of «{sc:lxxiv}» and of «{sc:lxxix}» stands apart like a point; a speck above the L of «{sc:lxxiv}» is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L24: «Wīǵan» has a bar over the i (2.3 by 1.1 points, measured with word_marks.py and read at 5,000 dpi) and the acute on the g; «al-Kūhī» has the bars over the u and the i.",
  "col_left L34: «Akhashwīros» has the bar over the i.",
  "col_left L35: «Yaḥyà» has the dot under the h and the grave on the last a; «Abī» the bar over the i; «Manṣūr» the dot under the s and the bar over the u.",
  "col_left L10, L36: the hyphens of «3-8» and «830-831» touch the figures on both sides; the bar between the 0 and the 8 is 4.0 points long, measured at 4,800 dpi (the free hyphens of this page are 1.9–3.7 points long, the en dashes of p. 401 5.4–5.6 points); compared at 6,000 dpi with the free hyphen in L14 of the right column, they look the same; read as hyphens.",
  "col_right L1: «Yaḥyà b. Muḥ.» has the dots under the h's and the grave; «Abī» and «al-Maghrabī» the bars over the last i; «’sh-Shukr» begins with the apostrophe of elision, and its hyphen is printed as a point at mid height (1.7 by 1.4 points); read as a hyphen.",
  "col_right L3, L30: «Isḥāq» has the dot under the h and the bar over the a; «al-Kindī» a round dot on its first i and the bar over the last.",
  "col_right L3, L4, L5: «Ya‘qūb» and «al-Ya‘qūbī» begin their second syllable with the sign of ‘ayn and have the bars over the u and the last i; «Ṭāriq» has the dot under the T, the bar over the a and a round dot on the i (1.6 by 1.6 points).",
  "col_right L6: «Yāqūt» has the bars over the a and the u.",
  "col_right L11: «*yātēd*» is printed in italics, with the bars over the a and the e. The Hebrew «יתד» is printed without vowel points, read at 8,000 dpi: yod, tav, dalet.",
  "col_right L12, L13: «*Yatīmat ad-dahr*» is printed in italics, with the bar over the i; «‘ālibī» begins with the sign of ‘ayn and has the bar over the a, a round dot on the first i and the bar over the last.",
  "col_right L14: «Yazdaǵird» has the acute on the g.",
  "col_right L17: «Yazīd» has the bar over the i.",
  "col_right L18, L19: «Yĕhūdāh» (twice) and «Shĕmū’ēl» have the breve on the first e, the bars over the u, the a and the second e and, in «Shĕmū’ēl», the apostrophe of the aleph; «‘Abbās» begins with the sign of ‘ayn and has the bar over the a.",
  "col_right L18: the right arm of the V of «{sc:xxxiv}» is printed broken, its top apart; a speck (0.6 by 0.6 point) under the baseline after it is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L20: «filius» is printed with the fi ligature.",
  "col_right L21: «Yōsēph» has the bars over the o and the e; «Elī‘ezer» the bar over the i and the sign of ‘ayin.",
  "col_right L22: «*yuga*» is printed in italics.",
  "col_right L23: «Yūsuf b. Tāshufīn» has the bars over the u, the a and the i.",
  "col_right L23, L24: a blank line separates the names in Y from those in Z.",
  "col_right L24: «Zakūt» has the bar over the u. The Hebrew «זכות» is printed without vowel points, read at 8,000 dpi: zayin, kaf, vav, tav.",
  "col_right L25: «Shādhān» has the bars over both a.",
  "col_right L26: «Zafi» is printed with the fi ligature.",
  "col_right L28: «az-Zamakhsharī» has the bar over the last i.",
  "col_right L29: «Zar’a» has the apostrophe of the hamzah; «Yā‘qōb» the bar over the a, the sign of ‘ayn and the bar over the o.",
  "col_right L30: «ar-Zarqālī» is printed so, with r in the article, read at 5,000 dpi, where the entries on pp. 380, 386, 407 and 409 have the assimilated z (az-Zarqālī); transcribed as printed. It has the bars over the a and the last i; «Abū» the bar over the u.",
  "col_right L33, L37, L40: the e of «eius» (L33), the second e of «variationem» (L37) and the e of «eo» (L40) are printed broken, their bars missing, like c; read e.",
  "col_right L40: «Arçachelis» is printed with ç.",
  "col_left, col_right: the ball terminals of the figures 3, 5 and 9 often stand apart (72 loose pieces with the real points, listed by loose_pieces.py); low on the line like points stand the lower balls of the 3s in «339», «39», «303», «293», «342», «312», «319», «335», «326», «283», «213», «310», «3», «325», «830-831», «344», «38», «313» and «293», and pieces of the feet of capitals in «J.» and «b.». None of them is a point.",
  "notes_left L1: the footnote continues the note (1) of p. 411. The rule over it (115.2 points long, from 267.4 to 382.6, at 731.7, across the column rule) lies 21 points below the last lines of the columns. Each line of the German quotation begins with a guillemet and a space, as printed.",
  "notes_right L2: the quotation closes with a space and a guillemet, «Pius ».»."
 ],
